WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.528
At the end of the Warring States period, Qin kept expanding outward.

00:00:03.878 --> 00:00:07.190
The small state of Yan felt a great threat.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:12.100
Qin's armies drew closer, step by step, to Yan's borders.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:17.802
Prince Dan of Yan asked Jing Ke to go to Qin on a dangerous mission.

00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:21.344
Jing Ke knew this journey was extremely dangerous, yet still agreed.

00:00:21.694 --> 00:00:26.014
On the day of departure, Prince Dan bid Jing Ke farewell at the Yi River.

00:00:26.364 --> 00:00:29.292
Everyone knew this might be a journey of no return.

00:00:29.642 --> 00:00:33.074
His friends sang a sorrowful, stirring song as they sent him across the river.

00:00:33.424 --> 00:00:36.712
Carrying the map, Jing Ke walked into the palace of Qin.

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:41.310
The palace was vast and silent, and the atmosphere was extremely tense.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:45.212
The youth Qin Wuyang, following him, trembled with nervousness.

00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:48.010
But Jing Ke's mission, in the end, did not succeed.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.408
He lost his life, while the King of Qin was unharmed.

00:00:51.758 --> 00:00:56.990
Later, Qin completed its wars unifying the six states.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.628
Jing Ke's story leads people to reflect on courage and loyalty.

00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:03.810
People remember his bravery, and feel sorrow for him.

